# LIGHT desktop package set — Orange Pi 4 LTS (Rockchip RK3399, arm64)
#
# A LEAN desktop, NOT the full Plasma+gaming stage4. Appended to packages.list
# by build-orangepi4-lts-stage4.sh UNCONDITIONALLY (this platform has ONE role — no
# --desktop light|none toggle the way Frite has one; every image built here is
# the light desktop). Sized for the Mali-T860 (Panfrost kernel driver / Mesa
# "panfrost" gallium driver — see make.conf.tmpl): X11 + a lightweight WM + a
# panel + a file manager + a terminal + a minimal browser. No KDE/GNOME/Plasma,
# no compositor-heavy Wayland session, no gaming stack. Mirrors
# specs-frite/portage/packages-light-desktop.list and
# specs-rpi5/portage/packages-desktop.list content 1:1 (same lean-LXDE recipe).

# ── Display server (X11; lean) ─────────────────────────────────────
x11-base/xorg-server
# Materializes the X drivers from INPUT_DEVICES=libinput + VIDEO_CARDS=panfrost
# (already unconditional in specs-orangepi4-lts/portage/make.conf.tmpl); without it
# Xorg has no input/video driver and the greeter is unusable.
x11-base/xorg-drivers
x11-apps/xrandr
x11-apps/xset
x11-apps/setxkbmap
x11-terms/xterm

# ── Desktop session: LXDE-lite (PCManFM + Openbox + LXpanel) ───────
# LXDE is the canonical "lean desktop": GTK-based, no compositor required, runs
# comfortably on any of the RAM SKUs these boards ship (4/8/16/32GB). Openbox is
# the WM; lxpanel the panel; pcmanfm the file manager; lxsession ties the
# session together.
x11-wm/openbox
lxde-base/lxpanel
lxde-base/lxsession
x11-misc/pcmanfm
lxde-base/lxappearance

# ── Login / session bring-up ───────────────────────────────────────
# LightDM is the lean display manager; on a single-user appliance you can also
# autostart Openbox from .xinitrc and drop lightdm — see RUNNING.md.
x11-misc/lightdm
x11-misc/lightdm-gtk-greeter
# The OpenRC `display-manager` init script does NOT ship with lightdm itself —
# it is provided by gui-libs/display-manager-init (configured via
# /etc/conf.d/display-manager DISPLAYMANAGER="lightdm", written by the
# builder). Without this the builder would enable a service the image never
# provides and the light-desktop image would boot to a bare console — this is
# the EXACT bug RPi5's Phase 3 review caught (missing lightdm.conf -> blank
# greeter); get it right from the start here (see build-orangepi4-lts-stage4.sh).
gui-libs/display-manager-init

# ── Minimal apps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
media-gfx/feh
app-editors/nano
# A minimal, modern browser. NetSurf is dramatically lighter than Chromium/
# Firefox and cross-compiles cleanly for arm64 — appropriate across the whole
# RAM SKU range these boards ship.
www-client/netsurf

# ── Fonts (so the lean desktop is legible out of the box) ──────────
media-fonts/dejavu
media-fonts/noto
